(# The two rows of small print that close a booklet: who built it, from what, and whose it is.

    They are the content of the last page's **footer** -- `base-booklet.jtex` boxes this once
    into `\dgsColophonBox`, the `colophon` page style puts that box above the page number, and
    `blocks/booklet/footer.jtex` reserves the box's own height under the credits. So this file
    is rows and nothing else: no rule, because the footrule is now the rule it used to draw for
    itself, and no page number, because that has to stay dynamic and cannot be frozen into a
    box built once in the preamble.

    The version of each repository is `git describe`, not the bare hash: on a tagged commit it
    is a name a reader can check out -- `29-final` -- and anywhere else it is the hash with the
    distance from the last tag in front of it, and `-dirty` behind it where the tree the build
    came from was not the tree the hash names. `blocks/metadata.jtex` carries the same facts
    into the file itself, with the exact hash alongside, for whoever has the PDF rather than
    the paper.

    The logo is the competition's own, the one the running head carries, and it is already a
    prerequisite of the document for that reason. `\raisebox` because a wordmark sits on its
    own baseline and the line it joins is 8pt: dropped by 0.8mm it reads as part of the
    sentence rather than as something floating above it.

    **Two lines of one paragraph, not two paragraphs.** A `\par` anywhere inside the argument
    of a macro that is not `\long` ends the scan, and the box is built inside `\sbox` within
    `\AtBeginDocument`, neither of which is long -- so the rows are separated by `\\`, which
    carries no such restriction, and the size is set once for both so that the `[1mm]` is
    measured against the type it separates.

    **The file must not end in `%`.** Jinja drops the trailing newline of an include, so a
    comment character on the last line would swallow whatever the including template writes
    next -- which is the brace that closes the box, and the error for that arrives pages away
    as `File ended while scanning use of \AddToHook`. #)
\fontsize{8}{10}\selectfont
{%
    (* i18n[language.id].competition.name.nominative *) (* volume.number *),
    (* language.id *) ((* language.name *)):
    booklet built by (* build.user *) with dgs \texttt{(* build.dgs.branch *)}: \texttt{(* build.dgs.describe *)}
    at (* build.timestamp.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S') *)
    from branch \texttt{(* build.repo.branch *)}: \texttt{(* build.repo.describe *)}%
}\\[1mm]
\raisebox{-0.8mm}{%
    \includegraphics[keepaspectratio = true, height = 3mm]%
        {build/(* module.id *)/(* competition.id *)/.static/logo/logo.pdf}%
}\hspace{1mm}%
\copyright{} (* competition.rights_holder *), (* volume.date.strftime('%Y') *).
\href{https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/}{CC BY-NC-SA 4.0}
